.TH tupdftext n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tupdftext
.PP
Text of a PDF, page by page, in pure Tcl. Meant for full\-text search: words, spaces and line breaks come out; columns and tables only as far as the order in the PDF gives them. No poppler, no C extension; the streams are unpacked with Tcl's built\-in \fBzlib\fR. A numeric-looking string from the page stays text (0.2).
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tupdftext 0.2
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tupdftext::pages   file ?-notext error|empty?
::tclutils::tupdftext::text    file ?-separator s? ?-notext error|empty?
::tclutils::tupdftext::summary file
.CE
.PP
\fBpages\fR returns a list with the text of every page, in page order. Lines are separated by \fB\en\fR, runs of blanks folded, ligatures (\fBﬁ\fR, \fBﬂ\fR, …) written out, soft hyphens removed.
.PP
\fBtext\fR joins the pages with \fB\-separator\fR (default form feed \fB\ef\fR, as \fBpdftotext\fR does).
.PP
\fBsummary\fR returns a dict:
.TS
l l.
Key	Meaning
\fBpages\fR	number of pages
\fBencrypted\fR	1 if the file has an \fB/Encrypt\fR entry
\fBversion\fR	header version, e.g. \fB1.7\fR
\fBtextPages\fR	pages with at least one character
\fBunmapped\fR	glyphs that came out as U+FFFD (two\-byte font without \fB/ToUnicode\fR)
\fBfonts\fR	list of dicts \fBname subtype toUnicode\fR for the fonts used
.TE
.PP
With \fB\-notext empty\fR a PDF without any text gives empty strings instead of the error \fBNOTEXT\fR.
.SS Errors
.PP
All errors carry \fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUPDFTEXT <kind>}\fR:
.TS
l l.
Kind	When
\fBFILE\fR	the file cannot be read
\fBFORMAT\fR	no \fB%PDF\-\fR header, no objects, or no pages
\fBENCRYPTED\fR	the file is encrypted (no decryption)
\fBNOTEXT\fR	no page has any text: a scan without OCR, or images only
\fBOPTION\fR	unknown option or missing value
.TE
.SS "What it reads"
.IP \(bu
\fBObjects\fR by scanning for \fBN G obj\fR at the start of a line. The cross\-reference table is not needed; a damaged one does no harm. A later definition of the same number wins, as with an incremental update. Objects in object streams (\fB/ObjStm\fR) fill in the numbers not defined directly.
.IP \(bu
\fBFilters\fR \fBFlateDecode\fR (also with PNG predictor), \fBASCIIHexDecode\fR, \fBASCII85Decode\fR, \fBLZWDecode\fR, and chains of them.
.IP \(bu
\fBPages\fR through the page tree from \fB/Root\fR, with inherited \fB/Resources\fR. Without a usable tree: all \fB/Type /Page\fR objects in file order.
.IP \(bu
\fBText operators\fR \fBTj TJ ' "\fR with \fBTf Tc Tw Tz TL Ts Td TD Tm T*\fR and \fBq Q cm\fR; Form XObjects (\fBDo\fR) with their own resources and matrix, up to depth 8, a form that draws itself is drawn once. Inline images are skipped.
.IP \(bu
\fBFonts\fR Type0 (two\-byte codes, \fBIdentity\-H\fR/\fB\-V\fR or an embedded CMap), Type1, TrueType, Type3. Unicode from \fB/ToUnicode\fR (\fBbfchar\fR, \fBbfrange\fR with offset or array), otherwise from \fB/Encoding\fR: \fBWinAnsiEncoding\fR, \fBMacRomanEncoding\fR, \fBStandardEncoding\fR, \fBPDFDocEncoding\fR, and \fB/Differences\fR with glyph names (WinAnsi names, \fBuniXXXX\fR, \fBuXXXX\fR, ligatures).
.IP \(bu
\fBSpaces and line breaks\fR from the positions in device space, with the glyph widths from \fB/Widths\fR, \fB/W\fR and \fB/DW\fR: a jump down by half a line is a new line, a gap of more than 0.15 em on the same line a space.
.SS "What it does not do"
.IP \(bu
decrypt (\fBENCRYPTED\fR), not even with an empty user password
.IP \(bu
read text from images (a scan needs OCR first)
.IP \(bu
map a two\-byte font without \fB/ToUnicode\fR (U+FFFD, counted in \fBunmapped\fR)
.IP \(bu
keep columns apart: text comes in the order of the content stream
.IP \(bu
join words hyphenated at the end of a line (\fBpdftotext\fR does)
.SS Measured
.PP
2026\-10\-21, Tcl 8.6.14 and 9.0.4, Linux. Words (letters and digits, lower case) compared with \fBpdftotext\fR (poppler 24.02): share of the pdftotext words that \fBtupdftext\fR also gives, and the other way round.
.TS
l l l l l l.
PDF	Producer	Pages	Time 8.6	pdftotext words found	own words in pdftotext
Tcl/Tk unter Windows	pdf4tcl 0.9.4.72, CID fonts	86	3.1 s	99.94 %	99.89 %
Tcl/Tk unter macOS	pdf4tcl 0.9.4.72	108	3.6 s	99.91 %	99.82 %
Debian unter Linux	pdf4tcl 0.9.4.72	32	0.9 s	99.94 %	99.87 %
DocIR handbook	pdf4tcl 0.9.4.72	9	0.3 s	100 %	100 %
same, \fBqpdf \-\-object\-streams=generate\fR	qpdf	9	0.3 s	100 %	100 %
same, \fBqpdf \-\-qdf\fR	qpdf	9	0.3 s	100 %	100 %
HTML book through LibreOffice	LibreOffice 24.2	150	3.6 s	99.79 %	99.57 %
DOCX through LibreOffice	LibreOffice 24.2	7	0.4 s	99.95 %	99.90 %
EuroTcl 2025 slides	PowerPoint (Microsoft 365)	27	1.2 s	100 %	100 %
Latin Modern info	xdvipdfmx, Type1	26	2.7 s	98.57 %	98.80 %
TeX Gyre Heros info	mbt PDF assembleur	33	3.6 s	99.49 %	99.56 %
math test (Word)	Ghostscript 9.02	1	0.04 s	91.18 %	91.18 %
math test (LuaLaTeX)	LuaTeX 0.70	1	0.04 s	90.62 %	96.67 %
.TE
.PP
The remaining differences: words hyphenated at a line end (pdftotext joins them), ligatures (written out here, a separate word for pdftotext), and the two\-dimensional layout of formulas. An encrypted file (\fBqpdf \-\-encrypt … 256\fR) gives \fBENCRYPTED\fR. Tcl 9.0.4 gives the same text as 8.6.14; characters outside the BMP come as one character on 9 and as a surrogate pair on 8.6.
.SS "Command line"
.CS
tclsh bin/tupdf.tcl text doc.pdf            # all pages, form feed between
tclsh bin/tupdf.tcl text doc.pdf -page 3
.CE
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tupdftext

# search a folder of PDFs, report the pages
proc pdfgrep {dir word} {
    foreach f [glob -nocomplain -directory $dir *.pdf] {
        if {[catch {::tclutils::tupdftext::pages $f} pages opts]} {
            puts "$f: [lindex [dict get $opts -errorcode] end]"
            continue
        }
        set n 0
        foreach p $pages {
            incr n
            if {[string match -nocase *$word* $p]} { puts "$f: page $n" }
        }
    }
}
.CE
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtclutils::tupdf\fR inspects the structure (version, objects, trailer, metadata, ZUGFeRD). \fBtupdftext\fR reads the text.
